rd on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, February to March came in at 55% of normal and March to April at 60% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18779 shows a preliminary August to September 2026 estimate of 68.7, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 18778 at 60% of normal.</p>"}
